---

<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="50–60 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson {page.sequence}</p>
  <h1>Zero conditional <em>when one situation regularly produces another</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Explain a dependable pattern, not a single prediction: <span class="ex">If the card reader flashes red, the door stays locked. When a customer changes the date, the system sends a new confirmation.</span></p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">50–60 min core</span>
    <span class="tag">if / when + present · present</span>
    <span class="tag">routines · systems · repeated results</span>
    <span class="tag">15–20 min listening and retrieval</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Find the repeated condition and the result that normally follows.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Connect meaning to present-simple form in both clauses.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Contrast</b><span>Separate a general pattern from one open future situation.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Explain a real or invented process and answer follow-up questions.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line"><b>Can-do:</b> By the end, you can explain repeated cause-and-result relationships, routines, system behavior, and standing procedures; form affirmative and negative Zero Conditionals; choose <span class="ex">if</span> or <span class="ex">when</span> from the intended meaning; order and punctuate both clauses; avoid presenting a limited pattern as a universal truth; and contrast a general Zero Conditional with a single open First Conditional.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved present-simple agreement, a repeated routine, and a direct instruction.">
    <h3>Three foundations from A1</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Use the subject, frequency expression, and sentence purpose.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Zero conditional foundation choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="sends">sends</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="send">send</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="usually">usually</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="yesterday">yesterday</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Press">Press</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Pressed">Pressed</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The singular subject system takes third-person present agreement: The system <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="sends" data-hint="System is singular, so the present-simple verb adds s." data-fix="The system sends a confirmation." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a confirmation.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The sentence describes a repeated routine, not one finished event: The support team <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="usually" data-hint="Usually marks a regular pattern." data-fix="The support team usually replies within an hour." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> replies within an hour.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Give the user a direct instruction with a base verb: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Press" data-hint="A positive imperative begins with the base verb press." data-fix="Press the blue button." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the blue button.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice a system that behaves the same way each time</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Harbor Workspace access guide</h3>
    <p><b>Normal entry:</b> <span class="ex">When a member scans an active card, the door unlocks.</span></p>
    <p><b>Expired card:</b> <span class="ex">If a card is expired, the reader flashes red.</span></p>
    <p><b>Missing reservation:</b> <span class="ex">If the system does not find a reservation, it sends the member to reception.</span></p>
    <p><b>Reception routine:</b> <span class="ex">When reception verifies the booking, the member receives a temporary pass.</span></p>
    <p><b>Important limit:</b> These sentences describe the documented behavior of this workspace system. They do not state universal facts about every access system.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Does each sentence describe one event tomorrow, or what regularly happens in a stated situation?</li>
      <li>Which clause states the condition? Which clause states its regular result?</li>
      <li>What tense appears in both clauses?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You identified the repeated condition, regular result, present-simple form, expected event, possible case, and evidence limit.">
    <h3>Discovery check: read the relationship</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Zero conditional discovery choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="repeated condition">repeated condition</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="regular result">regular result</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="present simple">present simple</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="expected repeated event">expected repeated event</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="possible repeated case">possible repeated case</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="this documented system">this documented system</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><span class="ex">When a member scans an active card</span> names the situation that activates the rest of the sentence, so it is the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="repeated condition" data-hint="This clause states the recurring situation that activates the result." data-fix="When a member scans an active card is the repeated condition." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><span class="ex">The door unlocks</span> states what normally follows that scan, so it is the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="regular result" data-hint="The second clause gives the normal consequence." data-fix="The door unlocks is the regular result." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The verbs <span class="ex">scans</span> and <span class="ex">unlocks</span> are both in the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="present simple" data-hint="Both verbs describe the system’s repeated behavior." data-fix="Scans and unlocks are present-simple forms." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The guide treats every normal active-card scan as part of the expected process, so <span class="ex">when</span> introduces an <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="expected repeated event" data-hint="When presents the scan as an expected stage in the repeated process." data-fix="When introduces an expected repeated event here." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>An expired card may or may not appear, so <span class="ex">if</span> introduces a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="possible repeated case" data-hint="If focuses on the cases in which the condition is true." data-fix="If introduces a possible repeated case." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The guide can support claims about <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="this documented system" data-hint="The evidence describes Harbor Workspace, not every access system." data-fix="The statements are limited to this documented system." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>, not every door and card reader in the world.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: a reusable relationship</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The name <span class="ex">Zero Conditional</span> is a teaching label, not a special verb tense. It describes a relationship the speaker presents as regular, dependable, or repeatedly observable. One situation creates the condition; another situation follows as its normal result.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>relationship</th><th>condition</th><th>regular result</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>system behavior</td><td><span class="ex">if the card is expired</span></td><td><span class="ex">the reader flashes red</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>work routine</td><td><span class="ex">when a client changes the date</span></td><td><span class="ex">we send a new confirmation</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>personal pattern</td><td><span class="ex">if I skip lunch</span></td><td><span class="ex">I get tired in the afternoon</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>rule or policy</td><td><span class="ex">if a payment arrives late</span></td><td><span class="ex">the account shows a late fee</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line"><b>Accuracy matters:</b> Grammar does not prove that a relationship is scientifically universal. <span class="ex">If I skip lunch, I get tired</span> reports a personal pattern. <span class="ex">If this reader detects an expired card, it flashes red</span> reports documented system behavior. The context defines how broad the claim is.</p>

  <h2>Build the core form</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The most useful core pattern uses the Present Simple in both clauses. Each verb agrees with its own subject.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>order</th><th>form and punctuation</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>condition first</td><td><span class="ex">If / When + present, present</span>; add a comma after the first clause</td><td><span class="ex">If the card expires, the reader flashes red.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>result first</td><td><span class="ex">Present + if / when + present</span>; normally no comma in this short pattern</td><td><span class="ex">The reader flashes red if the card expires.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>negative condition</td><td><span class="ex">if + do / does not + base</span></td><td><span class="ex">If the system does not find a booking, it sends an alert.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>negative result</td><td>present negative in the result clause</td><td><span class="ex">The door does not unlock if the card is inactive.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Do not add <span class="ex">will</span> simply because the result happens after the condition. The Zero Conditional presents the complete relationship as a standing pattern: <span class="ex">If the card is inactive, the door stays locked.</span></p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You controlled present-simple form, agreement, negatives, clause order, and punctuation in repeated relationships.">
    <h3>Drill 1: complete the repeated pattern</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Zero conditional form choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="scans">scans</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will scan">will scan</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="unlocks">unlocks</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will unlock">will unlock</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="doesn’t find">doesn’t find</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="won’t find">won’t find</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="sends">sends</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="send">send</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is">is</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="be">be</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="stays">stays</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="stay">stay</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The member is singular, so the condition needs present agreement: When a member <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="scans" data-hint="Member is singular, so use present scans." data-fix="When a member scans an active card, the door unlocks." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> an active card, the door unlocks.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The door is also singular, so its regular result uses <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="unlocks" data-hint="Use the present-simple result unlocks for the regular system behavior." data-fix="When a member scans an active card, the door unlocks." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The negative condition needs <span class="ex">doesn’t + base verb</span>: If the system <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="doesn’t find" data-hint="The singular system takes doesn’t, followed by base find." data-fix="If the system doesn’t find a reservation, it sends an alert." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a reservation, it sends an alert.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The singular system takes present agreement in the result: It <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="sends" data-hint="System is singular, so use sends." data-fix="It sends an alert if it does not find a reservation." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> an alert if it does not find a reservation.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The condition uses <span class="ex">be</span> in its present form for singular card: If a card <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is" data-hint="Card is singular, so the present form of be is is." data-fix="If a card is expired, the reader flashes red." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> expired, the reader flashes red.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The negative system result is a regular present pattern: The door <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="stays" data-hint="Door is singular, so use present stays." data-fix="The door stays locked if the card is inactive." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> locked if the card is inactive.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Choose if or when from the intended meaning</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>In repeated relationships, both words can be possible, but they focus attention differently.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>marker</th><th>usual focus</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">when</span></td><td>the event is an expected stage of the routine; think “every time this happens”</td><td><span class="ex">When reception verifies a booking, the member receives a pass.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">if</span></td><td>focus on the cases in which a condition is true; the case may not occur every time</td><td><span class="ex">If a card is expired, the reader flashes red.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p><span class="ex">When</span> does not make a statement more factual by itself, and <span class="ex">if</span> does not automatically mean “unlikely.” The surrounding situation and the speaker’s purpose determine the interpretation.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You chose when for expected repeated stages and if for possible cases, exceptions, and personal patterns.">
    <h3>Drill 2: frame the repeated situation</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="If and when choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="When">When</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="If">If</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="when">when</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="if">if</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="every expected stage">every expected stage</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="only the cases that match">only the cases that match</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Verification is a normal stage for every valid booking: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="When" data-hint="Use When to present verification as an expected repeated stage." data-fix="When reception verifies a booking, the member receives a pass." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> reception verifies a booking, the member receives a pass.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Only some cards are expired: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="If" data-hint="Use If to focus on the possible cases with expired cards." data-fix="If a card is expired, the reader flashes red." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a card is expired, the reader flashes red.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>A confirmation is a standard stage after every completed date change: The system sends a new confirmation <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="when" data-hint="When frames the completed change as the expected trigger." data-fix="The system sends a new confirmation when a customer changes the date." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a customer changes the date.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The guide describes the exception in which the screen has no connection: The app shows an offline message <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="if" data-hint="If focuses on the cases where the connection is unavailable." data-fix="The app shows an offline message if the screen has no connection." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the screen has no connection.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>In this guide, <span class="ex">when</span> helps the reader follow <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="every expected stage" data-hint="When organizes stages treated as normal parts of the process." data-fix="When helps the reader follow every expected stage." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>In this guide, <span class="ex">if</span> directs attention to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="only the cases that match" data-hint="If limits the result to cases where the stated condition is true." data-fix="If directs attention to only the cases that match the condition." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the condition.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Zero or First Conditional? Ask what time relationship the speaker means</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>speaker’s meaning</th><th>typical pattern</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>general, repeated, or standing relationship</td><td><span class="ex">if + present, present</span></td><td><span class="ex">If the reader detects an expired card, it flashes red.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>one open future condition and its response</td><td><span class="ex">if + present, will + base</span></td><td><span class="ex">If the reader flashes red tonight, I’ll call support.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>The condition clause can look similar because both patterns commonly use a present form after <span class="ex">if</span>. The result clause and time context reveal the difference. Compare <span class="ex">If clients change the date, we send a new confirmation</span>, a standing procedure, with <span class="ex">If Maya changes the date tomorrow, I’ll send a new confirmation</span>, one open future response.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You separated standing procedures and repeated effects from one open future response.">
    <h3>Drill 3: choose the time relationship</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Zero and first conditional contrast choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="stays">stays</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will stay">will stay</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="send">send</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will send">will send</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="get">get</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will get">will get</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="repeated relationship">repeated relationship</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="one open future response">one open future response</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The manual describes the reader’s normal behavior: If a card is inactive, the door <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="stays" data-hint="Use present stays for the standing system behavior." data-fix="If a card is inactive, the door stays locked." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> locked.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The team is discussing tonight’s one unresolved access problem: If this card is still inactive tonight, the door <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="will stay" data-hint="Use will stay for the predicted result in this one open future case." data-fix="If this card is still inactive tonight, the door will stay locked." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> locked.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>This is the company’s standing procedure: If clients change a booking date, we <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="send" data-hint="Use present send for the repeated procedure." data-fix="If clients change a booking date, we send a new confirmation." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a new confirmation.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Maya may change tomorrow’s booking, and you state your response: If Maya changes the date tomorrow, I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="will send" data-hint="Use will send for your response to one open future condition." data-fix="If Maya changes the date tomorrow, I will send a new confirmation." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a new confirmation.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>This is your recurring personal experience: If I skip lunch, I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="get" data-hint="Use present get for the recurring personal pattern." data-fix="If I skip lunch, I get tired in the afternoon." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> tired in the afternoon.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Tomorrow may be unusually busy, and you predict one consequence: If I skip lunch tomorrow, I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="will get" data-hint="Use will get for the result you predict in this one future case." data-fix="If I skip lunch tomorrow, I will get tired in the afternoon." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> tired in the afternoon.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Sound natural: make the condition and result easy to hear</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Say the sentence in two connected thought groups, with a small boundary between the condition and its result: <span class="ex">If the card is ex<strong>PIRED</strong> | the reader flashes <strong>RED</strong>.</span> Stress the key condition and the new result, not every word.</p>
  <p>In connected U.S. speech, <span class="ex">if the</span> often links smoothly as /ɪf ðə/, and unstressed <span class="ex">the</span> stays light. When the result comes first, keep the sentence moving into the final condition: <span class="ex">The reader flashes <strong>RED</strong> if the card is ex<strong>PIRED</strong>.</span> Use stronger contrastive stress only to repair a detail: <span class="ex">It flashes <strong>RED</strong>, not orange.</span></p>

  <h2>Read a troubleshooting guide carefully</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Desk 14 video-call setup</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">When a user signs in, the screen checks the camera and microphone. If the camera is unavailable, the camera icon turns orange. If another application controls the microphone, the sound test does not begin. When both tests finish successfully, the Join button becomes active. These are the normal results on Desk 14 with software version 6.2. Tomorrow the support team will install version 6.3. If the new version produces a different result, the team will update this guide.</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You recovered the documented process, condition-result relationships, evidence limit, and future contingency.">
    <h3>Reading check: use only the guide</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the screen checks the camera and microphone" data-hint="The first sentence states the normal result of signing in." data-fix="When a user signs in, the screen checks the camera and microphone."><p class="quiz-question">1. What normally happens when a user signs in?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the screen checks the camera and microphone">the screen checks the camera and microphone</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the support team installs new software">the support team installs new software</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the Join button immediately closes">the Join button immediately closes</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the camera icon turns orange" data-hint="Find the stated result of an unavailable camera." data-fix="If the camera is unavailable, the camera icon turns orange."><p class="quiz-question">2. What is the normal result if the camera is unavailable?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the camera icon turns orange">the camera icon turns orange</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the microphone becomes louder">the microphone becomes louder</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the Join button becomes active">the Join button becomes active</button></div></div>
